     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "\"Based on my search of Bupa's hospital cover documentation, here is what is included in the **Gold tier**:\\n\\n## Australian Government Hospital Tiers (Effective 1 July 2019)\\nBupa classifies private hospital covers into four tiers: Gold, Silver, Bronze, and Basic. These tiers use standard clinical definitions to make coverage easier to identify.\\n\\n## Gold Tier Benefits\\nThe Gold tier includes the following additional services beyond the minimum requirements:\\n\\n- **Accident Inclusion** (in addition to Silver tier)\\n- Various clinical categories covered under the Australian Government's hospital cover framework\\n\\n## Important Notes\\n- The four tiers do not apply to Visitors Hospital covers, Working/Non-Working covers, or Overseas Student Hospital covers\\n- An Eligibility Check should be undertaken prior to admission to confirm product coverage\\n- Specific products may have slight variations in clinical definitions or categories\\n\\n## Waiting Periods for Gold Tier\\n- 2 month initial waiting period\\n- Applies to: Palliative care, Hospital psychiatric services, and Rehabilitation\\n\\n## Excess Options Available for Gold Tier\\n- Nil (no excess)\\n- $250\\n- $500\\n- $750\\n\\n**Note:** The specific clinical categories included in the Gold tier beyond Accident Inclusion are not fully detailed in the available documents. For complete information about your specific Gold policy, I recommend:\\n1. Reviewing your policy documents directly\\n2. Contacting Bupa at 1300 663 590 (Mon-Fri 8:30am-5pm EST)\\n3. Checking with your hospital provider for coverage confirmation\\n\\nWould you like me to search for information about a specific aspect of your Gold tier coverage?\""
